#kaocha/v1
;; The unit lane discovers by DIRECTORY, and test/ now holds a second root
;; (test/raster, on the classpath only under -M:raster-test). Pointing the
;; suite at test/hive_schemas keeps discovery inside the one package this lane
;; can load — a bare ["test"] walks into test/raster and fails to require it.
{:tests [{:id          :unit
          :test-paths  ["test/hive_schemas"]
          :ns-patterns ["-test$"]}]}
